chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Bitcoin Core: the reference implementation, run and checked against the book"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the book's own source at tag third_edition_print1. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-09-28T22:08:15; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P_NOTES .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "How does chapter 3 of Mastering Bitcoin's 3rd edition take a reader from Bitcoin Core's source to a running full node and its programmatic interface, which of its steps, defaults and printed results still hold on the current release, and what does running the real software show that the book cannot?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-09-29." .
